#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128770 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "d180f745-028b-5859-8cad-4a49b5c20773" :question/math-academy-id "e-10521" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)( b_{j}+1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8 .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n  a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =(40-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (-8+18) \\\\  & =(10)\\cdot (10) \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128927 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/id #uuid "e17f982d-3d3e-5279-b507-d390e4f1970f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6116" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[(1+j)+(2+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j) & =(3+2\\cdot 1)+(3+2\\cdot 2)+(3+2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+7+9 \\\\  & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128928 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "e8f3608f-68f2-5ba9-b618-447887e7f6fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-6118" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  b_{ij} = 15.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}(1+2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}2{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2(8)-15 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1 & =5\\cdot 8+1 \\\\  & =40+1 \\\\  & =41.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "827c8e46-d0b0-5069-a187-6b461a964fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126417} {:answer/id #uuid "aceb1436-c191-5f85-87dc-5c27fd1e9567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126418} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b71b13-f56c-53ee-bd4e-1a63bfe35864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126419} {:answer/id #uuid "13743981-4143-5f77-b7c3-38e2482754ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126420} {:answer/id #uuid "484b317d-f202-5143-9eef-bee417679752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "484b317d-f202-5143-9eef-bee417679752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126421} :answer-field/id #uuid "def6dcec-0597-5a0d-82df-6c07ef5cf083" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "179c3108-3135-5849-a6a9-1775dfb4870a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149603" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}=10,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij}=20.\n$$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-10-20 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-30 & =5\\cdot 10-30 \\\\  & =50-30 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})=20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26a10fe3-3c44-5678-8753-7e01b7df09bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "130" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306721} {:answer/id #uuid "d6367fe5-a9a5-58b2-b3c4-bbc9c89b82e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306722} {:answer/id #uuid "c83a7605-aba5-555b-962e-e24f08a7bee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306723} {:answer/id #uuid "1d0028a4-d1bf-5b36-a0ec-61f70a4eda9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306724} {:answer/id #uuid "f72c58ae-4382-5b7c-bac8-0f38a40a5c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d0028a4-d1bf-5b36-a0ec-61f70a4eda9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306724} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f37c383-59c0-59e7-ba25-a8e19ba845d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38d56462-cbf1-5e86-b460-023450c63c10" :question/math-academy-id "q-149656" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}5({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{a}_{ij}=220,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{b}_{ij}=200.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}5({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) \\\\  & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{a}_{ij}-5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 220-5\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =1,100-1,000 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e687e59b-bd5e-5091-af45-549909da909a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "380" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306728} {:answer/id #uuid "c4551799-b919-5937-8bca-d4a013d31d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306729} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf11a1a-6320-56b5-b2e3-225cdc796ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306730} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ba6273-8d28-5cd6-8674-f7380ff8d525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "350" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306731} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4eb561-a931-55e4-8d26-794b52f181fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaf11a1a-6320-56b5-b2e3-225cdc796ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306730} :answer-field/id #uuid "2151875a-93a5-5122-9b63-f0ef4175404b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6977d60-a2ed-5069-b7de-47e979b8077a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149658" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}(3{a}_{ij}+4{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{a}_{ij}=50,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{b}_{ij}=55.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}(3{a}_{ij}+4{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}3{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}4{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{a}_{ij}+4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 50+4\\cdot 55 \\\\  & =150+220 \\\\  & =370.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306733 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b12b841e-010d-5f40-9611-b719716d0b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "130" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306735} {:answer/id #uuid "5297db7c-cae7-50cd-ac5f-402c45d9feaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306736} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca0fa06-3de7-523d-8346-b0993d420cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306737} {:answer/id #uuid "896a4d90-78cc-5707-a715-c85cb45179a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306738} {:answer/id #uuid "6313883d-5de0-5960-a31b-017f0e296ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b12b841e-010d-5f40-9611-b719716d0b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "130" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306735} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5ebd467-11c3-5f0a-b099-d5ff547fdae0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78a51fd9-8d34-52f1-82e6-e61ba25914f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-149661" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(1+{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{a}_{ij}=20,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{ij}=10.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(1+{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1)+20-10 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1)+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1)+10 & =10\\cdot 12+10 \\\\  & =120+10 \\\\  & =130.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(1+{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})=130.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a188518a-819c-5e89-a010-8674b6e34d2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306742} {:answer/id #uuid "398e8e8b-aff2-5edf-a956-678522685bea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306743} {:answer/id #uuid "32b618fd-84cb-5abd-b0af-d8616c1b7ae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306744} {:answer/id #uuid "afcf76d6-3dea-51ba-a7e4-9c1a168914ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306745} {:answer/id #uuid "71c0f49a-415f-5a0e-8c96-7cc657ba28aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a188518a-819c-5e89-a010-8674b6e34d2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306742} :answer-field/id #uuid "f03e86d1-ba0b-5a25-92d0-ef9f8b9fa24b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4326694-54aa-5ca1-8295-67918bfd804e" :question/math-academy-id "q-149676" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}=300,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}=250.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}2 \\\\  & =300+250-(2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) \\\\  & =550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) & =550-2\\cdot (15\\cdot 16) \\\\  & =550-480 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)=70.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac9d4a3-18ae-5718-b24c-7a3ce224ff56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306749} {:answer/id #uuid "16ac06ac-ef2e-5891-a039-c1186b2f57bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "280" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306750} {:answer/id #uuid "2817a337-b5e1-5a15-9e8a-356564571a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306751} {:answer/id #uuid "f4213ce7-177c-5378-9156-1647268250c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306752} {:answer/id #uuid "e413d5a4-5aa3-5824-a2b6-9c3a33942111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4213ce7-177c-5378-9156-1647268250c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306752} :answer-field/id #uuid "f83483bd-2e1f-5fe7-91af-41b8e7bb2cfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae7d8429-8a1e-525e-ab29-b8eebcd6061a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149689" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-5)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}=25,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}=58.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-5) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({b}_{j}-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({b}_{j}-5) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}5) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}-5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (58-5\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (58-50) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (8) \\\\  & =200\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f92600b6-ccdc-5f05-8549-91586156e7e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306756} {:answer/id #uuid "164ea086-02a6-5a61-85a3-304a248c6b26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306757} {:answer/id #uuid "89838c03-95f3-59de-8a38-78953c0c4256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306758} {:answer/id #uuid "2228c6dd-b6bb-5f23-8cfa-b729e1fdd585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306759} {:answer/id #uuid "82bdf342-b574-5c57-98aa-ece7bf7b1467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89838c03-95f3-59de-8a38-78953c0c4256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306758} :answer-field/id #uuid "b80a7566-9422-5319-b592-891744f3ed13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7bc6551-7fff-58fa-9ef3-72e47d44ac8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-149717" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}-1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{a}_{i}=20,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}=26.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}-1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}-1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{a}_{i}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}1) \\\\  & =(20+5)\\cdot (26-20) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (6) \\\\  & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0aa58bb-09c1-57bd-a2e8-443a33d0325f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "650" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306763} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd87c55-f528-5f51-b019-fb8343a51f11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "580" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306764} {:answer/id #uuid "35909a5d-6ade-5809-9f8a-94956bd5f512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "685" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306765} {:answer/id #uuid "c76c164d-6215-50fb-a9dd-02df62612f27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "450" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306766} {:answer/id #uuid "84220e2c-7b04-5da6-85bf-bd26bf21283c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "550" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c76c164d-6215-50fb-a9dd-02df62612f27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "450" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306766} :answer-field/id #uuid "19805f7c-461d-5261-b208-cf35a1a47788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2c66ce3-c438-54c0-aeee-a7bc3e19f9fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-149726" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}({a}_{i}-4)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}=85,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}=18.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}({a}_{i}-4) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}({a}_{i}-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}({a}_{i}-4) & =(5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}4) \\\\  & =(5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}1) \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 18)\\cdot (85-4\\cdot 20) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (85-80) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (5) \\\\  & =450\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94ec8758-a34c-547a-8bce-755804178aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "325" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306770} {:answer/id #uuid "aac5a646-8fbc-50d2-a52b-4f31207ba7f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "335" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306771} {:answer/id #uuid "3aba4c03-2240-57cd-b904-eab60d584d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306772} {:answer/id #uuid "c79714c0-634d-56f8-b317-4ff6f523c7b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306773} {:answer/id #uuid "a4fffd85-7b5a-5872-8a69-91e62aa52bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "355" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94ec8758-a34c-547a-8bce-755804178aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "325" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306770} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4b8a93-fb1b-55c8-9887-1e0897c985c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4825646e-446d-5585-9d07-aa29f475bcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-149736" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}=20.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}3) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}1) \\\\  & =(35-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (20+3\\cdot 15) \\\\  & =(35-30)\\cdot (20+45) \\\\  & =(5)\\cdot (65) \\\\  & =325.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc027ffe-d94e-5d37-b4b0-fc7f18a78bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306777} {:answer/id #uuid "0b4a80b4-a39d-58ee-936f-932bcf84eac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306778} {:answer/id #uuid "68c8c636-971f-5556-8a9d-791975673631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306779} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b8b217-6b0d-5040-9c79-b96b213c5a96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306780} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb24593-fc32-5d2f-be15-e598753e98b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb24593-fc32-5d2f-be15-e598753e98b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306781} :answer-field/id #uuid "951b85e6-1c14-5271-b183-c7d040b076c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "197b91db-85fc-55db-a755-0d996363fe0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-149742" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-6)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}=15,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}=68.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-6) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}({b}_{j}-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}({b}_{j}-6) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}6) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}-6{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}1) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (68-6\\cdot 11) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (68-66) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f0586c1-f847-5f1d-813e-201ffbe3602d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128517} {:answer/id #uuid "ca27efbb-d8e9-5672-8d49-b940e1529e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128518} {:answer/id #uuid "fe993036-0c8e-5ce9-a4aa-6fa757b16e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128519} {:answer/id #uuid "2070c5bc-e29d-59d5-8976-d2cacdfb4944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128520} {:answer/id #uuid "3df57c7a-2f3b-5d4a-b683-5d5f484e8511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca27efbb-d8e9-5672-8d49-b940e1529e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128518} :answer-field/id #uuid "4063a526-a4d9-5833-b289-1a70432dda9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e16a192-c647-58f3-9bd2-bc5597aebc2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-72094" :question/problem "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(1j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j & =6\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6+12 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "896ea1ff-cb31-59a5-a401-a764ffa812a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306784} {:answer/id #uuid "34013482-073d-579e-854a-e37119c01bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "79" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306785} {:answer/id #uuid "33b85747-9397-50b4-a900-f04a281ce9c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306786} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1fded8-cdf1-53a7-9028-1019989f85b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306787} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd4bc82-046c-5669-8ac6-2bbb7b4afeb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34013482-073d-579e-854a-e37119c01bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "79" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306785} :answer-field/id #uuid "95e660a7-06c4-5604-bd22-895d9933dded" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ddbc322-5143-51b3-a11b-3d2aa2c354f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-72397" :question/problem "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2} & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2}) & =((1+1)^{2}+(2+1)^{2}+(3+1)^{2})+((1+2)^{2}+(2+2)^{2}+(3+2)^{2}) \\\\  & =(4+9+16)+(9+16+25) \\\\  & =79\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0793e41-473b-531a-8459-af35e76b4424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306791} {:answer/id #uuid "4b47e142-f6dc-54b8-a809-f7fe0f8175be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306792} {:answer/id #uuid "701fe059-8630-5e16-967